id: recipe.rest-api
kind: recipe
title: REST API service
aliases: rest api, http api, crud service, stateless http service
question: how would you design a REST API service?
tags: architecture, api, http
properties:
  - horizontal scaling (stateless replicas)
  - zero-downtime deploys
  - bounded latency via timeouts
  - observability per route
invariant: Each request is independent; all state lives in a database or cache, so replicas are interchangeable.
answer_30s: Stateless HTTP handlers behind a Service, one shared connection pool, typed errors mapped to status codes, timeouts on every outbound call, and readiness-driven rolling updates.
flow: |
  Client
     |
  Ingress (TLS, routing)
     |
  Service -> Deployment: Rust/Axum replicas (stateless)
     |
  Connection pool -> Database
     |
  (read path: Redis cache)
compose:
  - k8s.deployment => replicas are declared and converged, so scaling is a number change
  - k8s.probe.readiness => only replicas that can serve are in the endpoint list
  - rust.axum => typed extractors map input to handlers and errors to status codes
  - rust.app-state => one state value carries the pool, clients and config without globals
  - rust.connection-pool => the database sees a bounded, reused set of connections
  - rust.error-enum => client errors and upstream errors map to distinct status codes
  - design.timeouts => every dependency call has a deadline derived from the request budget
  - design.health-checking => readiness decides which replicas receive traffic
  - design.observability => request rate, errors, duration and saturation per route
  - k8s.service => stable name in front of changing pods
  - k8s.deployment.rolling-update => new version replaces the old without dropping requests
failure_modes:
  - state kept in process memory, so one replica serves a different answer than another
  - no timeouts on outbound calls, so a slow dependency exhausts the pool
  - 500 returned for validation errors, hiding real failures in the error rate
follow_ups:
  - where would you put pagination and caching?
related:
  - rust.axum
  - rust.app-state
  - recipe.database-backed-api
  - recipe.cache-backed-api
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/axum/latest/axum/
